  "findings": [
    {
      "topic": "Scope and current source",
      "decision": "ACCEPT",
      "facts": "One existing Host Emulated workflow is sufficient. The frozen current preimage is the independently fetched Plan60 blob4211a5b6, with132 lint and72 artifact operands. Plan59 only changes unrelated general CI/staging sources; root must recheck the actual publication parent. All18 retained helper/dependency bytes match the prior official209a records; this review does not claim a new remote fetch of every dependency. The eight journey helpers already occur in the declared proof roster. No helper, product, test, public API or new framework is selected."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Closed selection and no genuine Claude/Codex",
      "decision": "ACCEPT",
      "sources": [
        "desktop-proof-mode.ts:222-232,330-342",
        "desktop-proof-fixture.ts:139-206",
        "desktop-backend-fixture.ts:99-100",
        "desktop-backend-smoke.ts:110-126"
      ],
      "facts": "The four new explicit Darwin ARM64 rows select the existing OpenCode V2 lifecycle modes. The existing V2 fixture and model switch exclude genuine Claude/Codex. Empty Quit selector is invalid; the plan correctly requires absence except pending-open warm, and clears it for cold. All modes stay outside general Ready/full-qualification activation."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Reuse and guard preservation",
      "decision": "ACCEPT",
      "facts": "The four existing Review steps can be shared through closed static descriptors and one proof-owner switch. Existing Review/common assertions,132 lint operands and unrelated management Settings/C8 bytes remain required exact preservation gates. One original warm invocation and only selected original external cold invocation occur; Resume already owns its two epochs. Receipt/log data never selects a mode or path. This is a document-level design approval; actual afterimage preservation must be independently reviewed."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Compiled epoch identity",
      "decision": "ACCEPT",
      "sources": [
        "desktop-captured-app.ts:557-565,680-694,711-768",
        "desktop-backend-observations.ts:428-441"
      ],
      "facts": "The top-level compiled array and firstEpoch array refer to the first epoch. Original code copies those exact files to cold-resume-epoch1-bundles, records the first pins and verifies copied bytes. compiledBundleHashes recursively accepts this directory and emits relative .js/.cjs hashes, so it is an existing suitable data reader. SecondEpoch pins bind current dist. firstEpoch has no status field; first normal cleanup, writer release, distinct app group/Host PID and checkpoint/history witness are the real boundary."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Quit and pending custody",
      "decision": "ACCEPT",
      "sources": [
        "desktop-native-quit-ui-smoke.ts:148-156,165-206,305-346,370-427",
        "desktop-backend-smoke.ts:317-342,617,682-700"
      ],
      "facts": "Both Quit routes reach the common Quit/finally, so quitRequested=true is required for every outer receipt. Active input unknown or terminal cancelled/failed and queued cancelled without dispatch remain the original oracle. Pending-open legitimately permits held/unknown open-unknown debt despite physical absence; the plan preserves that disjunction and does not erase unresolved custody. Cold Quit has no nativeInputsReplayed/originalReceiptSha256 fields; environment/cold metadata joins provide the actual warm SHA binding."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Checkpoint Resume",
      "decision": "ACCEPT",
      "sources": [
        "desktop-resume-ui-smoke.ts:51-59,285-330",
        "desktop-resume-records.ts:98-138",
        "desktop-captured-app.ts:711-768"
      ],
      "facts": "The original route has one explicit Resume, one continuation and second Stop. It checks two released generations, same native session, original history prefix,11 observations, final detached/released restoration and recovery snapshot. History SHA covers bounded ordered native-session serialization, not whole SQLite bytes. The plan does not add a fresh Launch or transfer this positive to full Windows W07."
    },
    {
      "topic": "PNG journey",
      "decision": "ACCEPT",
      "sources": [
        "desktop-native-chat-attachments-ui.ts:20-44,106-132,197-211",
        "desktop-composer-ui-smoke.ts:159-185,203-281"
      ],
      "facts": "The selected V2 branch permits one PNG file input and returns before text Download logic. The original model verifies three second-turn requests carry the prepared image hash. Original helper checks preview2x1/SHA, attachment references without path/base64 exposure, two Sends, completed native Task, ONE/TWO effect, durable native image history and Stop before Quit. The plan preserves those actions and their original deadlines."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Metadata and no replay",
      "decision": "ACCEPT",
      "sources": [
        "desktop-opencode-v2-cold-metadata.ts:98-141,149-193,373-386",
        "desktop-opencode-metadata-lineage.ts:existing assertDesktopMetadataLineageRetained"
      ],
      "facts": "Warm Review, warm Quit/PNG, first Resume Host, second Resume Host and cold readback have different existing proof owners. The plan correctly uses those owners, including ready/opening rather than invented PASS and firstMetadataAbsentBeforeSecondSpawn rather than the generic final flag. The one read-only cold metadata child is separate from zero Runtime allocation, and its original lineage/physical closure remain required."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Artifacts and budgets",
      "decision": "ACCEPT",
      "facts": "The exact eight additions produce80 unique artifact operands with72 unchanged prefix; selected SQLite namespace is bounded and WAL/SHM may be absent. Original screenshot globs cover all selected names. No native input rehash claim is inferred from Codex-only selectedNativeInputHashes arrays. Existing45-minute row/5-minute aggregate and native/UI/cleanup deadlines remain unchanged; no guaranteed fit or runtime acceptance is claimed."
    }
